1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,386
This is my bedroom in Istanbul.

2
00:00:03,386 --> 00:00:09,557
RiskLens flagged the wardrobe with
suitcases on top, and it says what

3
00:00:09,557 --> 00:00:14,700
it can't see: whether it's anchored is
unknown, not assumed.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:21,767
In Istanbul, earthquake preparation
includes what is inside our homes.

5
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:28,880
Film one room for under a minute, or
upload a video.

6
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:34,700
Or try one of four samples, no filming
needed.

7
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:40,366
Here is a live run, with the waiting
shortened.

8
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:48,246
Muse Spark looks at sampled frames and
plans which objects matter in this room.

9
00:00:48,246 --> 00:00:55,000
SAM 3.1 tracks each of those objects
through the whole video, so

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,191
every finding points to a real frame and a
real box.

11
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:07,946
Then Spark surveys the marked frames,
separating what is visible from what

12
00:01:07,946 --> 00:01:14,700
needs checking, and looks up FEMA E-74
guidance for the next steps.

13
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:22,970
Every finding shows what the video shows
and what is still unknown.

14
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:30,639
Each next step links to the FEMA section
the model actually read;

15
00:01:30,639 --> 00:01:36,391
if that source check fails, no
instructions are shown.

16
00:01:36,391 --> 00:01:44,700
Muse Image can illustrate a
recommendation, always labelled as
AI-generated, never as proof.

17
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:50,476
After a fix, you re-film the item.

18
00:01:50,476 --> 00:01:57,130
Uploading the same video again cannot
prove anything changed.

19
00:01:57,130 --> 00:02:04,524
That check is a file hash, before any
model call.

20
00:02:04,524 --> 00:02:09,700
Real before-and-after validation is still
future work.

21
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:16,530
I also designed three Istanbul rooms with
hazards placed on purpose, made

22
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:21,721
with Muse Image and checked view by view
with Spark.

23
00:02:21,721 --> 00:02:27,951
RiskLens matched five of five, four of
four, and four of five,

24
00:02:27,951 --> 00:02:31,585
missing a blocked path to the door.

25
00:02:31,585 --> 00:02:34,700
Designed scenes, not an accuracy claim.

26
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:40,843
RiskLens is a visual screening tool, not a
building inspection.

27
00:02:40,843 --> 00:02:47,494
It finds the evidence, is honest about
what it cannot see, and

28
00:02:47,494 --> 00:02:54,700
helps you decide what needs a closer look,
one room at a time.
